        "document_id": "1862",
        "explanation": "Sens. Baucus and Tester explicitly state, 'The Senators announced today that $12.5 million for vital military projects in Butte has been included in the Defense Appropriations Bill,' directly attributing the funding to their efforts."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely discusses, critiques, or supports an issue, policy, or outcome without explicitly linking it to their own actions or efforts. General statements of support, criticism, or advocacy for a cause or position do not constitute credit-claiming unless the senator takes personal ownership of a specific result. Additionally, statements that focus on the actions of others (e.g., the administration, other senators, or external entities) without attributing the outcome to the senator’s own work are not credit-claiming.",
